<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Sidicini</h1><p class="st-meta">600 BCE – 334 BCE (approx.) · capital Teanum Sidicinum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Oscan people of northern Campania whose appeal for help against the Samnites in 343 BCE set off Rome's first war with Samnium.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Sidicini lived around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teanum-sidicinum">Teanum Sidicinum</a> (modern Teano) in the hills between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roccamonfina">Roccamonfina</a> volcano and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volturno">Volturno</a>, bordering the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aurunci">Aurunci</a> and Campanians. They were an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a>-speaking people, possibly related to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samnite-league">Samnites</a> or the Ausones; their earlier history is unknown.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known mainly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, they formed a small community centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teanum-sidicinum">Teanum</a>, which later issued its own coins in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oscan-language">Oscan</a>. In 343 BCE the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/samnite-league">Samnites</a> attacked them; the Sidicini sought help from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/capua">Capua</a>, and Capua's appeal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-samnite-war">First Samnite War</a>. They joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latins">Latins</a> and Campanians against Rome in 340 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cales">Cales</a> on land taken from the Sidicini and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aurunci">Aurunci</a> in 334 BCE, ending their independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teanum-sidicinum">Teanum Sidicinum</a> became a Roman ally and later a municipium and colony.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sidicini.jpg" alt="Sidicini" width="320" height="346"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Samnium.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 BCE – 334 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Teanum Sidicinum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Oscan polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oscan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-467&amp;focus=sidicini" aria-label="Sidicini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4922 598 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sidicini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5242 854h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5242 854h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Italy. <a href="/atlas?year=-467&amp;focus=sidicini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

